+## 2. Mechanism synthesis for the admin lane
+
+The verdict plane currently exhibits TWO failure modes that produce "closed" states decoupled from reality:
+1. **Verdict-null auto-resolve**: issues close with latestVerdict null, verdictHistory empty, no landed label (#2225 pre-reopen; #2738 now).
+2. **Label-derived verdicts**: a label correction (bookkeeping) generates an APPLIED_LABEL_DERIVED verdict, which then functions as closure authority (#2736) even when the fix is verifiably absent.
+Both bypass the only closure semantics that track reality: verification evidence (merged fix / file-on-main / runtime probe). Remedy direction (admin): (i) auto-resolve must write an explicit verdict naming its reason; (ii) label corrections must be bookkeeping-only — never verdict-generating on fix-pending rows; (iii) APPLIED_LABEL_DERIVED should require a verification pointer (run/commit/hash), not a label alone; (iv) closure of evidence-chain issues (#2738-class) should require the subject's terminal state, not a claim TTL expiry.
